1
00:00:00,869 --> 00:00:04,079
(Sheldon:)Besides disrupting the local gravity field.

2
00:00:05,082 --> 00:00:07,872
(Leonard:)If he were any bigger,
he'd have moons orbiting him.

3
00:00:08,043 --> 00:00:10,293
- Oh, snap.
- Ha-ha.

4
00:00:10,963 --> 00:00:13,043
(Sheldon:)So I guess we'll be leaving now.

5
00:00:13,215 --> 00:00:14,965
(Leonard:)Why should we leave?

6
00:00:15,134 --> 00:00:18,764
(Leonard:)For all we know, he crashed the party
and Penny doesn't even want him here.

7
00:00:20,431 --> 00:00:22,851
You have a backup hypothesis?

8
00:00:23,016 --> 00:00:24,936
Maybe they just wanna be friends.

9
00:00:25,477 --> 00:00:29,437
(Sheldon:)Or maybe she wants to be friends
and he wants something more.

10
00:00:29,606 --> 00:00:31,356
(Leonard:)Then he and I are on equal ground.

11
00:00:31,525 --> 00:00:34,815
(Sheldon:)Yes, but you're much closer to it
than he is.

12
00:00:36,071 --> 00:00:40,281
(Leonard:)Look, if this was 15,000 years ago,
by virtue of his size and strength...

13
00:00:40,451 --> 00:00:43,161
(Leonard:)...Kurt would be entitled
to his choice of female partners.

14
00:00:43,328 --> 00:00:46,328
(Sheldon:)And male partners, animal partners,
large primordial eggplants...

15
00:00:46,498 --> 00:00:48,998
(Sheldon:)...pretty much
whatever tickled his fancy.

16
00:00:49,585 --> 00:00:52,255
(Leonard:)Yes, but our society
has undergone a paradigm shift.

17
00:00:52,421 --> 00:00:56,671
(Leonard:)In the information age, Sheldon,
you and I are the alpha males.

18
00:00:56,842 --> 00:00:59,342
- And we shouldn't have to back down.
- True.

